<title>USA: U.S. weekend box office chart -- July 4-6.</title>
<headline>U.S. weekend box office chart -- July 4-6.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1997-07-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following are the final data for the top 10 movies at the July 4-6 box office, according to Exhibitor Relations Co.</p>
<p>    Film			Three-day gross    Cumulative Gross</p>
<p> 1. Men in Black		 $51,068,455	 $ 84,133,900</p>
<p> 2. Face/Off		     $16,067,233	 $ 51,521,285</p>
<p> 3. Hercules		     $12,193,152	 $ 50,030,540</p>
<p> 4. My Best Friend's Wedding $10,818,090	 $ 69,281,429</p>
<p> 5. Batman &amp; Robin	     $ 8,027,257	 $ 90,716,119</p>
<p> 6. Out to Sea		   $ 5,887,675	 $  ----</p>
<p> 7. Con Air			$ 3,791,861	 $ 85,073,453</p>
<p> 8. The Lost World	     $ 2,604,420	 $218,334,199</p>
<p> 9. Wild America		 $ 1,810,586	 $  ----</p>
<p> 10 Speed 2: Cruise Control  $ 1,517,680	 $ 41,113,064</p>
<p>NOTE: &quot;Men in Black&quot; is released by Columbia Pictures, a unit of Sony Corp.. Sony's TriStar studio released &quot;My Best Friend's Wedding.&quot;</p>
<p>&quot;Face/Off&quot; is released by Paramount Pictures, a unit of Viacom Inc..</p>
<p>&quot;Hercules&quot; and &quot;Con Air&quot; are released by Walt Disney Co..</p>
<p>&quot;Batman &amp; Robin&quot; and &quot;Wild America&quot; are released by Warner Bros, a unit of Time Warner Inc..</p>
<p>&quot;The Lost World: Jurassic Park&quot; is released by Universal Studios, a unit of Seagram Co. Ltd..</p>
<p>&quot;Out to Sea&quot; and &quot;Speed 2: Cruise Control&quot; are released by 20th Century Fox, a unit of News Corp..</p>
